<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ladislaus Kán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1315">1315</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ladislaus III Kán</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ladislaus Kán was voivode of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> from about 1294 until his death in 1315 and one of the great oligarchs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> at the end of the Árpád dynasty. He ruled Transylvania almost as an independent prince and in 1307 seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-of-thorns">Holy Crown</a> from the claimant Otto of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, refusing to surrender it to Charles I until 1310.</p></div>
